## Data Flow

### Starting a Process

```
User Request
    ↓
UnifiedEngine.start_process_from_bpmn()
    ↓
[1] Get AI startup advice (optional)
    ↓
[2] BPMNEnginePersistent.deploy_process()
    ↓ ProcessRepository.create()
    ↓ PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO workflow.bpmn_processes
    ↓
[3] BPMNEnginePersistent.start_process()
    ↓ InstanceRepository.create()
    ↓ PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO workflow.bpmn_instances
    ↓
[4] Parse BPMN → Find start events → Create initial tasks
    ↓ TaskRepository.create() for each task
    ↓ PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO workflow.bpmn_tasks
    ↓
[5] Publish event: bpmn.instance.started
    ↓
[6] Event handler: Track in Workflow Intelligence (optional)
    ↓
Return instance_id
```

### Completing a Task

```
User completes task
    ↓
UnifiedEngine.complete_task(task_id, variables)
    ↓
BPMNEnginePersistent.complete_task()
    ↓
[1] TaskRepository.complete(task_id)
    ↓ PostgreSQL: UPDATE workflow.bpmn_tasks SET status='completed'
    ↓
[2] InstanceRepository.update_variables() - Merge variables
    ↓ PostgreSQL: UPDATE workflow.bpmn_instances SET variables = variables || ...
    ↓
[3] Parse BPMN → Find next activities
    ↓
[4] Create next tasks OR mark instance as completed
    ↓
[5] Publish event: bpmn.task.completed
    ↓ Event handler: Track in Workflow Intelligence
    ↓
[6] If instance completed: Publish bpmn.instance.completed
    ↓ Event handler: Collect case for learning
```

### AI Recommendations

```
BPMN task created
    ↓
Event: bpmn.task.created
    ↓
UnifiedEngine event handler
    ↓
_get_task_recommendations(task_id, activity_id)
    ↓
[1] Get instance context
    ↓
[2] Apply rule-based recommendations (module-specific)
    ↓
[3] (Future) Call AI Advisor for ML-based recommendations
    ↓
[4] BPMNEnginePersistent.update_task()
    ↓ TaskRepository.update_ai_recommendations()
    ↓ PostgreSQL: UPDATE workflow.bpmn_tasks SET ai_recommendations = ...
    ↓
Task now has AI recommendations injected
```

